    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 26 October 2005, the erection of a detached outbuilding measuring a width of 8m, a length of 16m and a height of 3.8m at the ridge and 2.6m at the eaves, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the outbuilding takes up less than 50 percent of the original garden area and is less than 4m in height within 2 metres of the boundary.  \r\n"
